 "notes": "Fifth-force/ISL review by Adelberger, Heckel & Nelson (Eot-Wash group), Annu. Rev. Nucl. Part. Sci. 53 (2003). Curve = lower boundary of the 95% CL 'excluded region' (yellow) in Fig.5 (midlam.eps, 1 um<lambda<1 cm) in the Yukawa |alpha| vs lambda plane, combining the group's own Eot-Wash torsion-balance limit (dominates the deep minimum ~1e-2 near lambda~1e-3 m) with Irvine, Colorado, Lamoreaux/Moscow and Stanford limits forming the envelope. Extracted directly from EPS vector polygon vertices (CFN-filled yellow regions). Axis calibration from tick marks: x 3.440->15.440 cm = lambda 1e-6->1e-2 m (3 cm/decade); y 2.100->12.897 cm = |alpha| 1e-4->1e10 (0.7712 cm/decade). Converted to boson mass via m[eV]=1.97e-7 eV*m / lambda[m]; |alpha| reported in native units (Yukawa strength relative to gravity), no canonical g_N conversion attempted. Envelope is the union of experimental heavy curves; at large lambda (~1e-2 m) Irvine takes it to ~5e-4, mid-range plateau ~1e-2 is Eot-Wash, small-lambda rise is Stanford/Colorado. dm_density null (not a DM search).",
